// TurboQuant combo for -ctk turbo4 -ctv turbo4 (added by hand, not autogenerated by generate_cu_files.py).
// Needed for the nvfp4 competitor gate: turbo4_0 storage (66 B / 128 coords = 0.5156 B/coord) is the PPL rival.
// NOTE: default routing still sends turbo4 combos to the f16-scratch MMA path (GGML_TURBO_DITHER speed gate
// in fattn.cu); this instance only makes the native vec kernel AVAILABLE (GGML_CUDA_FATTN_VEC_NATIVE=1).
// CORRECTED 2026-11-03: the old "runs past ~8K only this way / MMA needs 8.0 GiB f16 scratch at 32K" claim was
// WRONG. The f16 scratch lives inside the ggml scratch pool of the FA op itself (fattn-common.cuh
// get_f16_extra_data: ggml_nelements of the K/V views, whose ne[1] is the CURRENT n_kv) and the pool is reused
// by every op in the graph. Peak = one op's K+V: 134 MiB at 32K, ~0.48 GiB at 120K - 120K contexts run fine
// with the scratch path on a 16 GB card (observed in production, no OOM). The native vec path buys decode
// speed, not VRAM.  No 64 case: a QK_TURBO4 = 128 block does not fit in a 64-element K row.

#include "../fattn-vec.cuh"

DECL_FATTN_VEC_CASE(128, GGML_TYPE_TURBO4_0, GGML_TYPE_TURBO4_0);
DECL_FATTN_VEC_CASE(256, GGML_TYPE_TURBO4_0, GGML_TYPE_TURBO4_0);
